*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Scratch git worktrees an agent session creates to work in isolation. They are real
# checkouts of this repository, so committing one makes it an embedded repo that a clone
# cannot fetch — and they are disposable by construction.
.claude/worktrees/

# Convex agent skills are installed twice — once into .claude/ for Claude Code and
# once into .agents/ for the generic convention. We only use the former, so the
# duplicate is ignored. Regenerate either with `npx convex ai-files install`.
.agents/

# Convex
# Note: convex/_generated/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Committing it keeps
# `npm run build` and a fresh clone typechecking without running the Convex CLI
# first. Convex regenerates it on every dev/deploy anyway.
# The deployment URL and dev deploy key live in .env.local, covered by .env.* above.

# ⚠️ **PRODUCTION SNAPSHOT EXPORTS. NEVER COMMIT ONE.** A Convex backup zip is every
# table verbatim — every game's DM code and recovery hash, every NPC stat block, every
# scene name and every private feed line, none of it filtered by the queries that exist
# to filter it. This repository is public and its bundle is readable (CLAUDE.md
# invariant 1), so a committed backup publishes in one file everything the whole guard
# apparatus exists to withhold, and rewriting history afterwards does not un-publish it.
#
# Kept out by directory rather than by extension, because the next export will be saved
# somewhere with a different name and the thing to make safe is the habit of putting
# backups here.
convex_backups/
